{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"Before calling arbitrage “failed,” compare the ETF’s closing price with a synchronized, executable portfolio-value estimate—not stale NAV or last-trade-based indicative value. Account for fair-value adjustments, time zones, closing-auction effects, and holdings that stop trading before the ETF.\n\nReview intraday patterns and different market closes; compare peers with similar holdings, benchmarks, and trading hours. Assess spreads, depth, volatility, creation/redemption costs, settlement constraints, and the tradability of underlying securities. Ask APs and market makers about quoting, inventory, hedging, and creation/redemption activity, including any decline or concentration in participation.\n\nUse independent data and interviews before concluding. Potential responses include clearer disclosures, better valuation or trading data, liquidity-provider outreach, or operational changes. Monitor in context rather than relying on a single numerical trigger."}}
